1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,622
Hello, I'm DiGi. This one's for you and your grown up.

2
00:00:05,622 --> 00:00:08,496
Snuggle up. Ready?

3
00:00:08,636 --> 00:00:12,789
Before we start, let's do our big breath.

4
00:00:12,789 --> 00:00:15,403
Breathe in, and out.

5
00:00:15,403 --> 00:00:16,997
Lovely.

6
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:21,888
Now, thinking caps on. Remember our last adventure?

7
00:00:21,888 --> 00:00:25,217
Some screen things are pretend.

8
00:00:25,217 --> 00:00:29,303
So when we're not sure if something on a screen is real,

9
00:00:29,303 --> 00:00:30,998
what do we ask?

10
00:00:30,998 --> 00:00:35,491
That's right. We ask, "Is this real?"

11
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:37,298
Clever you.

12
00:00:37,298 --> 00:00:42,719
Well, today we find something on the screen

13
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:47,298
that is real. Very, very real.

14
00:00:47,298 --> 00:00:50,459
Today we learn one big thing.

15
00:00:50,459 --> 00:00:57,436
The words you send on a screen land on a real person's feelings.

16
00:00:57,436 --> 00:01:00,403
So we choose kind words.

17
00:01:00,403 --> 00:01:03,427
Say our special word. Kind.

18
00:01:03,427 --> 00:01:08,236
Just four little letters. K, I, N, D.

19
00:01:08,236 --> 00:01:10,043
Look at this phone.

20
00:01:10,043 --> 00:01:13,848
The screen looks like glass, doesn't it?

21
00:01:13,848 --> 00:01:16,869
But here's a little secret.

22
00:01:16,869 --> 00:01:20,105
It isn't glass at all. It's a window.

23
00:01:20,105 --> 00:01:26,069
And on the other side of the window, there's a real person.

24
00:01:26,069 --> 00:01:29,106
A real friend with a real heart.

25
00:01:29,106 --> 00:01:31,569
A friend who giggles.

26
00:01:31,569 --> 00:01:36,508
Who gets happy and sad and everything in between.

27
00:01:36,508 --> 00:01:38,919
Just like you.

28
00:01:38,938 --> 00:01:42,805
Now watch what happens when you type a word.

29
00:01:42,805 --> 00:01:43,672
Hi.

30
00:01:43,672 --> 00:01:47,948
The word doesn't stay on the glass. Oh no.

31
00:01:47,948 --> 00:01:52,619
It folds itself into a tiny paper plane

32
00:01:52,619 --> 00:01:54,802
and it flies through the window

33
00:01:54,802 --> 00:01:57,719
all the way to the real person.

34
00:01:57,719 --> 00:02:02,224
And it lands right on their feelings.

35
00:02:02,224 --> 00:02:08,869
Kind words land warm, like a hug, like sunshine.

36
00:02:08,924 --> 00:02:11,020
Now, one more true thing,

37
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:14,473
because you're big enough to know it.

38
00:02:14,473 --> 00:02:18,528
Most people on the other side of the window are kind.

39
00:02:18,528 --> 00:02:20,806
Most planes land warm.

40
00:02:20,806 --> 00:02:23,097
But some people send unkind words,

41
00:02:23,097 --> 00:02:27,074
and some people pretend to be someone they are not.

42
00:02:27,074 --> 00:02:30,741
A bit like dressing up, but not for fun.

43
00:02:30,741 --> 00:02:34,415
If that ever happens, you don't have to fix it.

44
00:02:34,415 --> 00:02:37,185
You just tell your grown up.

45
00:02:37,185 --> 00:02:45,090
Telling is never naughty, and it is never, ever your fault.

46
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:46,629
Pause me here.

47
00:02:46,629 --> 00:02:50,096
Grown up, ask your little one:

48
00:02:50,096 --> 00:02:52,666
when someone says something kind to you,

49
00:02:52,666 --> 00:02:55,338
how does it feel in your tummy?

50
00:02:55,338 --> 00:02:58,707
Have a little chat. I'll wait.

51
00:02:58,707 --> 00:03:01,981
Here's how a chat like this can sound.

52
00:03:01,981 --> 00:03:07,875
A child might say, "I like it when my friend says well done."

53
00:03:07,875 --> 00:03:10,415
And the grown up says, "Me too.

54
00:03:10,415 --> 00:03:13,875
It makes me feel happy right here."

55
00:03:13,875 --> 00:03:15,229
And guess what?

56
00:03:15,229 --> 00:03:19,288
Your kind words do the same for other people,

57
00:03:19,288 --> 00:03:22,454
even through the screen.

58
00:03:22,713 --> 00:03:24,841
You have a superpower.

59
00:03:24,841 --> 00:03:28,419
Every day you get to pick your words,

60
00:03:28,419 --> 00:03:30,953
little paper planes,

61
00:03:30,953 --> 00:03:34,992
flying from your heart to somebody else's.

62
00:03:34,992 --> 00:03:38,056
So we pick the warm ones,

63
00:03:38,056 --> 00:03:42,670
because a real person catches every single plane.

64
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:44,899
And here's the helper part.

65
00:03:44,899 --> 00:03:48,862
If someone on a screen is unkind to your friend,

66
00:03:48,862 --> 00:03:51,170
you can be the helper.

67
00:03:51,170 --> 00:03:54,354
You don't join in. You tell a grown up,

68
00:03:54,354 --> 00:03:58,470
and you send your friend something extra kind.

69
00:03:58,470 --> 00:04:02,327
So the warm planes outnumber the cold ones.

70
00:04:02,327 --> 00:04:05,031
Helpers are heroes.

71
00:04:05,404 --> 00:04:08,268
Pause me again. Grown up, ask:

72
00:04:08,268 --> 00:04:13,204
who could we send a kind message to right now?

73
00:04:13,204 --> 00:04:16,163
Pick one person you both love.

74
00:04:16,163 --> 00:04:18,517
I'll be right here.

75
00:04:18,517 --> 00:04:24,193
So when we look at a screen, what do we remember?

76
00:04:24,193 --> 00:04:29,099
Say it with me, three times. Big voices!

77
00:04:29,099 --> 00:04:31,548
Real person on the other side.

78
00:04:31,548 --> 00:04:33,891
Real person on the other side.

79
00:04:33,891 --> 00:04:36,757
Real person on the other side.

80
00:04:36,757 --> 00:04:40,251
And here's the little bit that goes with it.

81
00:04:40,251 --> 00:04:44,503
If someone is unkind, that is never your fault.

82
00:04:44,503 --> 00:04:47,335
Go and tell.

83
00:04:47,603 --> 00:04:50,607
Tonight, here's the fun bit.

84
00:04:50,607 --> 00:04:54,770
Together, send one kind message

85
00:04:54,770 --> 00:04:59,317
to Grandad, to a cousin, to a friend.

86
00:04:59,617 --> 00:05:01,090
It can be tiny.

87
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:05,330
"I love you." "You are the best."

88
00:05:05,784 --> 00:05:09,142
Or just a big smiley face.

89
00:05:09,150 --> 00:05:14,687
Send it from your grown up's phone, snuggled up together.

90
00:05:14,687 --> 00:05:17,997
Then watch what happens.

91
00:05:17,997 --> 00:05:22,635
Somewhere, a real person will smile,

92
00:05:22,635 --> 00:05:26,703
because your kind word just flew through the window

93
00:05:26,703 --> 00:05:30,255
and landed right on their heart.

94
00:05:30,869 --> 00:05:37,494
Before I go, show your grown up one thing you remember from today.

95
00:05:37,494 --> 00:05:40,035
Anything at all.

96
00:05:40,035 --> 00:05:43,593
Got it? Brilliant.

97
00:05:44,169 --> 00:05:49,506
And grown up, one kind message tonight.

98
00:05:49,506 --> 00:05:53,018
Remember, screens are better together.

99
00:05:53,018 --> 00:05:54,682
See you next time.
